# E2 (PLAN_ENTERPRISE_REGRESSION.md): pure UI-only backfill for the product detail page — every
# scenario in `tests/mixed/storefront.tflw` that reaches this page immediately does something else
# on it (add to cart, open a frame, …); this isolates the page itself: reached via a real catalog
# row link (not a hardcoded `open "/products/{id}"`), showing name/price/stock and nothing more. No
# `api` step in the test body (decision 5) — the seed catalog already has a stable, uniquely-named
# product to search for.

@ui @catalogOps
test "opening a product from its catalog row shows its name, price, and stock"
  open "/"
  fill field "Search" with "Mechanical Keyboard"
  click text "Mechanical Keyboard"
  within css "#product-heading"
    expect text "Mechanical Keyboard" is visible
  expect text "$79.99" is visible
  expect text "40 in stock" is visible
